Well, I did it, finally added an S to my ascention list.  I really don't
know why I had so much trouble with them before, they really seem to be
tanks.  I ran around with a +0 Snikersnee and -10 AC until I was at medusa.
About that point was when I finally identified ?oID, figured out how to
enchant armor and weapons.  Once my AC was at a more reasonable level, I
dropped my shield in favor of #twoweaponing with my starting Katana.


My original plan was to sacrifice until I got Grayswandir and then
#twoweapon that with a silver saber.  Many turns later, I had a large
collection of useless artifacts, and then I decided it was time for
something different.  So I decided it would look better for a Samurai to use
Katanas, instead of silver sabers.  After a midgame wish (from a throne,
IIRC) I got +3sdsm.  Everything else in the dungeon was provided.  I grabbed
the /oW at the castle, and at the time the only thing I could think of to
wish for were boots of speed.  I stashed the wand temporarily, and headed
into Gehennom.  About 3 levels down, I found an elf who wasn't wearing elven
boots.  Turned out he had boots of speed, so that solved that.  On dlvl 44,
the RNG decided to mock me by randomly generating another /oW on the ground.
Grrr....

So, this ascention was an achievment for me, because it was my lowest number
of wishes ever.  If only I could have gone wishless.


The trip out of G-Land was uneventful, the mysterious force hit maybe twice,
and didn't throw me more than a level.  The wizard only showed up at the
scantum (double trouble there),  once more in the dungeon, and fianlly on
the plane of earth.  I'm not sure, but this might have been my lowest number
of encounters with him ever.

The hardest part about my ascention run was an odd event with terrible
consequences.  I was in Geryon's lair (thanks heck^2!!) and having trouble
getting to the stairs up.  So I zapped myself with a /oT, which, instead of
teleporting me, exploded, and blew up my only =oLevitation (and a couple
other wands and such).  Must have been cursed huh?

Got past Juiblex's lair with a c!oGL, passed the castle and Medusa's the
same way.  I was on the plane of earth when I realized I only had 3
?oGoldDetection, so I figured I'd just search for the portal on air, and use
them on the rest.


It was on Air that I realized that I had no means of levitation.  Well,
except for a single !oLevitation I happened to have.  So I blessed it,
quaffed it, and ran.  Some enemy on Air was kindly enough to find the portal
for me.  Fire's portal was really close to where I entered, so I was able to
fly to it while still levitating.  Wandered around water for a looong while.
Made it to astral, hit the middle (famine) but that was chaotic.  So I went
toward death, and that turned out to be the right one.  This time I
remembered to summon my guardian angel, only to find that it had been
killed.  Oh well.

